{{!--
  PRELOADER v4 — minimal instant-text preloader.

  Sequence (see assets/js/preloader.js):
  1. This text is visible the instant the DOM parses it — no JS wait, no
     fade-in delay. #particles-load-scrim (particle-morph.hbs) is already a
     full-viewport opaque layer covering the page from t=0, so the text sits
     on that scrim rather than needing its own background here.
  2. preloader.js sets window.__preloaderRunning = true (so
     particle-morph.hbs's own scrim auto-fade backs off — see that file's
     "if (!window.__preloaderRunning)" gate) and soft-fades .preloader-text
     in.
  3. After a short hold, preloader.js fades BOTH .preloader-text and the
     shared #particles-load-scrim out together, then dispatches
     preloader:done — same contract prior preloader versions used
     (window.__preloaderSkipped / __preloaderDoneFired / 'preloader:done'),
     so main.js, page-transition.js, scroll-scrub-anim.js,
     particle-morph-system.js and particle-animation-loop.js all keep
     working unchanged.

  Previous version (wordmark letter-reveal / dot-bounce / particle globe
  burst) was already DEAD CODE — its Preloader class was never invoked;
  the file's real path (hidePreloader()) hid everything instantly with no
  visible animation at all. This is the first real preloader visual since
  that was disabled.
--}}

<section id="preloader" class="preloader">
  {{!-- Indeterminate — no aria-valuenow on purpose (WAI-ARIA: omit it when
        the duration isn't known). ONE streak (.progress-bar-streak) — see
        main.css's comment on .progress-bar-streak/bar-comet-shoot for the
        current "comet/shooting star" motion design. .progress-bar-streak and
        the .progress-bar-track marker are SHARED with .scroll-progress
        (default.hbs) — same animated-bar system reused for page-to-page
        navigation, not a preloader-only component (see page-transition.js).
        The streak is duplicated TWICE — once in .progress-bar-clip (crisp,
        clipped to the track), once in .progress-bar-glow (identical,
        blurred, stacked on top) — see main.css's comment on those two
        classes for why a real duplicate layer, not box-shadow, and why it
        has to live outside the clip. --}}
  {{!-- is-loading is hardcoded here, not toggled by JS: unlike
        .scroll-progress (which doubles as the real scroll indicator and so
        must be switched in and out of the loading state), this element
        exists ONLY during loading — there is no "off" state to return to. --}}
  <div class="preloader-progress-bar progress-bar-track is-loading" id="preloader-progress-bar" role="progressbar" aria-valuetext="Loading" aria-label="Loading">
    <div class="progress-bar-clip">
      <div class="progress-bar-streak"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="progress-bar-glow" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="progress-bar-streak"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="preloader-content">
    <h4 class="preloader-text" id="preloader-text">Opportunity lives in complexity</h4>
  </div>
</section>
